###Alert #8

**Alert Title:** SOC141 - Phishing URL Detected
**Date:** 2021-03-22T21:23:12+03:00
**Severity:** High
**Source IP:** 172.16.17.49
**Destination IP:** 91.189.114.8
**Type:** Proxy
**Event ID:** 86

###Hypothesis:
An internal user(ellie / 172.16.17.49) navigated to a suspicious URL hosted on a compromised external web serever(91.189.114.8) via proxy, indicating potential exposure to a credential harvesting phishing campaign.

###Evidence :
- Destination Hostname: mogagrocol.ru
- Full Requested URL: http://mogagrocol.ru/wp-content/plugins/akismet/fv/index.php?email=ellie@letsdefend.io
  The main domain(ogagrocol.ru) belongs to a legitimate agricultural college website in Russia that was hacked.
- Hidden Fake Folder: The path /wp-content/plugins/akismet/fv/index.php shows that attackers hid a malicious script inside a legitimate WordPress plugin folder(akismet). The unknown /fv/ directory was manually created by the attackers to host a fake login screen.

###Classification Decision:
True Positive (User Clicked). Confirmed phishing URL navigation by internal user ellie(172.16.17.49). Proxy logs confirm the request was allowed, verifying the user clicked the link and established a connection to the external phishing server.

###Summary of Findings:
An alert (SOC141 - Phishing URL Detected) was triggered when internal host EmilyComp (172.16.17.49, user ellie) requested a known phishing URL on external host mogagrocol.ru (91.189.114.8).
Analysis confirms the link contained a tailored query parameter (?email=ellie@letsdefend.io) pointing to a hidden directory on a compromised WordPress site. The proxy action was allowed, confirming user interaction.

###Recommended Actions 
Immediate Containment: Block mogagrocol.ru and 91.189.114.8 at the perimeter proxy/firewall.

Identity Protection: Force an immediate password reset and revoke active session tokens for user ellie@letsdefend.io in case credentials were submitted on the page.

Endpoint Verification: Run a full EDR scan on EmilyComp (172.16.17.49) to check for drive-by file downloads or secondary payload execution.

Email Security: Search email gateway logs for the subject line or sender of the phishing message and purge it from all internal user inboxes.
